Fixed. The bug was in `advanceTurn` at `src/sim.ts:43`.

The condition was `if (foodSurplus >= 0)`, which grew population by 1 even when food production exactly equaled consumption (surplus of 0) — exactly the "barely breaking even" case playtesters reported. Changed it to `if (foodSurplus > 0)`, so population only grows on a genuine surplus, matching the function's docstring ("grows by 1 if there was a food surplus this turn").

Verified: `npm run test` passes (4/4) and `npm run typecheck` passes.


